
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A few years back, I <a href="https://dailynous.com/a-little-logic-each-day-semantics-too/">posted</a> about the &#8220;Daily Logic&#8221; and &#8220;Daily Semantics&#8221; project of <a href="https://sites.google.com/site/joshdeverphilosophy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Josh Dever</a>, professor of philosophy at the University of Texas at Austin.</p>



<span id="more-26341"></span>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="730" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-1024x730.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-26342" style="aspect-ratio:1.4027584732171496;width:568px;height:auto" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-1024x730.jpg 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-300x214.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-768x547.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-1536x1094.jpg 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2-250x178.jpg 250w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/logic-envelope-tiny-2.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The projects offer up mini-lessons in logic or semantics that anyone can subscribe to. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the time, Professor Dever wrote, &#8220;The idea of each is that each day you get sent a little, roughly 200 word bite in the relevant area, so that you can gradually and painlessly(-ish) build up real expertise.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Since that post, Professor Dever has added over 2000 more logic lessons and several hundred more semantics lessons to the services. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The lessons are pitched at roughly the &#8220;grad student new to the area&#8221; level.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anyone can sign up for the lessons at the respective sites: <a href="https://dailylogiclessons.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Daily Logic</a> and <a href="https://daily-semantics-app.onrender.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Daily Semantics</a>. </p>
